Each path below is a runnable example.

## See the whole system

The rooms app is the fullest demonstration: several language bindings, a
browser UI, live chat, and direct messages created by a three-party handoff.

```sh
zig build rooms-web-iroh
```

Open `http://localhost:8000`, pick a member, and choose **Message**. The room
introduces the two members and then leaves their conversation path.

Native peer-to-peer traffic rides encrypted
[iroh]($link.page('transports/iroh')) there, so the command needs Cargo for the
transport sidecar as well as Deno. There is a Deno-only
`zig build rooms-web-tcp` that serves the same page over cleartext TCP, which
authenticates no peer and carries CapTP in the clear. For the standardized
Goblins path over Tor, `zig build demo-rooms-onion` runs one hosted service and
two independent clients (needs Deno, Tor, and outbound network).

## Learn the Zig API

Start with
[01_connect_and_serve.zig](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/examples/zig/01_connect_and_serve.zig).
It shows both ends of one TCP conversation: listen, publish, connect, fetch,
and call.

```sh
zig build examples
```

Two later chapters isolate the capability moves that are easiest to miss:

- [02_introduce_and_redeem.zig](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/examples/zig/02_introduce_and_redeem.zig)
  hands a capability to a third peer and leaves the introducer behind.
- [06_pipeline_and_attenuate.zig](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/examples/zig/06_pipeline_and_attenuate.zig)
  calls through an unresolved promise and wraps a capability with a smaller
  interface.

The [complete example guide](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/examples/README.md)
continues down through actors, bootstrap lookup, and the raw engine.

## Embed from C

[host_embedder_pump.c](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/examples/c/host_embedder_pump.c)
is the first C program to read. It drives two byte-fed `PancakeHost` instances
through the sole C CapTP application surface. Continue with
[the C guide](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/consuming-from-c.md)
for linking, ownership, the host allocator, and transport composition.

## Try another application

| App | What it shows | Run |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [tasks](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/apps/tasks/) | Shared task state across peers | `zig build demo-tasks` |
| [tools](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/apps/tools/) | Delegation, attenuation, and revocation | `zig build demo-tools` |
| [accountability](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/apps/accountability-on-pancake/) | Signed calls above an OCapN session | `zig build demo-accountability` |

Tasks and tools need Deno. Accountability runs a Zig host with Deno and Python
callers. The same applications also serve as binding examples; the
[bindings overview]($link.page('bindings')) points to each language.
